---
// STORY — short founders page (handoff §8): Vacaville, father & son,
// built in the USA by Pure Sports Technologies (partner, not owned facility).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import QuoteBlock from '../components/QuoteBlock.astro';
import EmailCapture from '../components/EmailCapture.astro';
import FooterTicker from '../components/FooterTicker.astro';
---
<Base title="SOLID. — Story">
  <main>
    <Nav current="story" />

    {/* the ONE stadium-black section on this page */}
    <section class="story-hero">
      <img class="story-photo" src="/assets/lifestyle_field.png" alt="" />
      <div class="story-hero-copy">
        <div class="story-eyebrow">FROM THE DUGOUT ▸ VACAVILLE, CALIFORNIA</div>
        <h1>A FATHER, A SON,<br />AND A BINDER OF CARDS.</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="story-body">
      <p class="story-lede">
        We grew up ripping wax packs in the garage — sorting rookies on the
        carpet, trading doubles at school, checking corners like they were
        gold. The cards mattered because they were <em>numbered</em>. Because
        somebody else wanted the one you had.
      </p>
      <p>
        Solid started in Vacaville, California, with a father and son asking a
        simple question: what if a bat brand worked the way a card set did?
        Numbered runs. No reprints. A card in every box with a serial that
        matches the bat in your hands.
      </p>
      <p>
        And one more rule, the one that makes it Solid: every edition is
        dedicated to a cause. Twenty-five dollars from every bat, totals
        published, receipts on file. Not a portion of proceeds. A number you
        can check.
      </p>
      <p>
        The bats are built in the USA by our manufacturing partner,
        <strong>Pure Sports Technologies</strong> — ASA and USSSA certified,
        made to get ripped in a Tuesday-night league, not displayed in a case.
        The card is the collectible. The bat is for swinging.
      </p>
    </section>

    <QuoteBlock />
    <EmailCapture />
    <FooterTicker />
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .story-hero {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--stadium-black);
    overflow: hidden;
    min-height: 480px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
  }

  .story-photo {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: var(--photo-hero);
  }

  .story-hero-copy {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    padding: 80px 48px 48px;
  }

  .story-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-kinetic);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--red);
    background: var(--cream);
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 4px 10px;
  }

  .story-hero-copy h1 {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5.5vw, 72px);
    color: var(--hero-text);
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .story-body {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 72px 24px;
  }

  .story-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--navy-2);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .story-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif) !important;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 22px !important;
    color: var(--navy) !important;
    line-height: 1.55 !important;
  }

  .story-body strong { color: var(--navy); }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .story-hero-copy { padding: 56px 20px 32px; }
    .story-body { padding: 48px 20px; }
  }
</style>
